249
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:28,600
Iura was doing his job
and you guys <i>weren't</i> ?

250
00:01:28,810 --> 00:01:31,150
Oh, I've got this CD!

251
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:35,520
Wait, really?! This must've been one
I forgot to give back to you. Sorry.

252
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:38,190
Oh, snap, yeah, I'll take it.

253
00:01:38,190 --> 00:01:39,480
Sorry, man.

254
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:42,520
Come to think of it, I have
some DVDs I borrowed off you.

255
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,350
Huh?

256
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:44,900
Same here.

257
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:46,310
What?

258
00:01:46,310 --> 00:01:49,020
Well, there goes my sweet,
light-handed commute.

259
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:50,440
Sorries!

260
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:51,940
All good.

261
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:55,650
You still have way more
than all of us, Yuki.

262
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:58,810
A couple of us stronger guys could
help you carry it down to the entrance.

263
00:01:58,810 --> 00:02:01,650
Like me, Ishikawa, or...

264
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:04,400
...Hori- <i>san</i> !

265
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:08,480
What'd I do?!

266
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:11,100
H-He means you're so dependable, Hori- <i>san</i> !

267
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:14,900
He didn't mean anything insulting by it!

268
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:38,760
Horimiya

269
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:49,040
I Would Gift You The Sky

270
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:51,560
Remi, could you get the trash...?

271
00:03:52,290 --> 00:03:55,290
Fun Spring Trips!

272
00:03:52,290 --> 00:03:55,290
Fun Spring Trips!

273
00:03:53,190 --> 00:03:56,150
She's distracted again.

274
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:58,150
What're you reading? A travel mag?

275
00:03:58,150 --> 00:03:59,520
Uh-huh.

276
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,400
Is that a zoo?

277
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:04,900
You wanna go see a big herd of giraffes?

278
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,650
I mean, sure, but...

279
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:10,190
Sengoku- <i>kun</i> , Yanagin!
You wanna go to the zoo, too, yeah?

280
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:12,600
Which one? The same one as before?

281
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:16,020
No, a different one.

282
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:19,650
Whoa, this is pretty far away.
We'd have to make it a two-day trip.

283
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:21,060
We'd need a car.

284
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:22,810
And a hotel.

285
00:04:22,810 --> 00:04:25,850
So we can go if we get a car and a hotel?!

286
00:04:25,850 --> 00:04:27,520
Don't encourage her, boys.

287
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:29,900
You're going to make her
think this might actually happen.

288
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:30,520
She's such a mom.

289
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,900
Okay, mom.

290
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:34,480
A car, though... Sure
would be nice to have one.

291
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,310
We could get to way more places.

292
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:38,810
I can't wait to get my license.

293
00:04:38,810 --> 00:04:40,230
Huh?

294
00:04:40,230 --> 00:04:44,690
If I had a car, I could take you anywhere
you wanted, Remi, not just that zoo.

295
00:04:44,690 --> 00:04:48,480
O-Oh. Yeah, that's right.

296
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:53,400
Perhaps this isn't about going
to the zoo, but something else?

297
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,600
What do you mean?

298
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:57,190
I'm gonna go buy a drink!

299
00:04:57,190 --> 00:04:58,770
Hold it, Remi.

300
00:04:58,770 --> 00:05:02,020
What's going on? What's bothering you?

301
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,020
Nothing!

302
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:04,940
We won't know unless you tell us.

303
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:07,560
Grab her, Sengoku- <i>kun</i> .

304
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:09,650
It's nothing, I swear!

305
00:05:09,650 --> 00:05:11,230
So tell us what it is.

306
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:13,230
H-Hey, uh...

307
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:15,940
If you won't let us help you,
then you're going to force my hand.

308
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:19,100
I'll show Yanagi- <i>kun</i> what you look
like with your cheeks all stretched out.

309
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,770
K-K-Kono- <i>san</i> ?!

310
00:05:20,770 --> 00:05:22,770
Fine, do it! Get it over with!

311
00:05:22,770 --> 00:05:24,230
Ayasaki- <i>san</i> ?!

312
00:05:24,230 --> 00:05:27,310
What on Earth is going on?!
Is this something you do often?!

313
00:05:27,310 --> 00:05:29,100
Certainly you can't force
her to talk like... like...

314
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:32,770
Oh, wow, her cheeks...

315
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:35,560
Kono- <i>san</i> , Ayasaki- <i>san</i>
can't talk like this!

316
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,650
Sengoku- <i>kun</i> , please make her stop!

317
00:05:37,650 --> 00:05:40,850
Take a good, long look. You don't
get to see her like this that often.

318
00:05:40,850 --> 00:05:43,350
Why?!

319
00:05:43,350 --> 00:05:44,850
Are you okay?

320
00:05:44,850 --> 00:05:48,190
I'm fine. That felt nice.

321
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:50,020
It did?

322
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:54,310
Look, it's not bothering me or anything.

323
00:05:54,310 --> 00:06:01,100
I just figured we could go somewhere
fun while we're still in high school.

324
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:05,060
But as soon as you talked
about getting a license,

325
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:10,400
I realized he could use it
to go really far away.

326
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:13,270
Or he could just use it
to do everyday errands.

327
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:14,930
Getting a car = going away???

328
00:06:13,270 --> 00:06:16,100
Oh...

329
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:17,940
Fun Spring Outings

330
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:19,480
I mean, we don't have to go
to the zoo or anything.

331
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:22,650
You don't need to worry.
We'll be friends forever.

332
00:06:22,650 --> 00:06:26,560
Really? You won't treat me like
a stranger the second you graduate?

333
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:29,730
Not at all. That'd be a lot
of effort on our part.

334
00:06:29,730 --> 00:06:30,560
Here's an idea.

335
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,020
Huh?

336
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:35,310
Once I get my license, would you
all like to go on a road trip?

337
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:37,020
That sounds nice. Where would we go?

338
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:38,810
L-Let's go to the ocean!

339
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:40,770
Are you fond of the ocean, Kono- <i>san</i> ?

340
00:06:40,770 --> 00:06:43,850
I-I wanna go to the ocean, too!
We can go swimming!

341
00:06:43,850 --> 00:06:47,230
I won't swim. I just
want to see the ocean.

342
00:06:47,230 --> 00:06:50,230
Then that's what we'll
do after graduation.

343
00:06:52,350 --> 00:06:55,230
Let's go to the zoo, too, Yanagin!

344
00:06:55,230 --> 00:06:57,480
Why don't you get your
license, too, Ayasaki- <i>san</i> ?

345
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,060
Because I call shotgun!

346
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:00,520
No fair, Remi!

347
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:02,940
Sengoku- <i>kun</i> ...

348
00:07:04,810 --> 00:07:06,690
Hori- <i>san</i> ?

349
00:07:06,690 --> 00:07:09,150
Earth to Hori- <i>san</i> ...

350
00:07:11,770 --> 00:07:14,190
She's fast asleep.

351
00:07:14,190 --> 00:07:18,690
Makes sense after carrying
all that heavy stuff.

352
00:07:18,690 --> 00:07:19,770
Miyamura.

353
00:07:19,770 --> 00:07:22,730
Yeah! I'm here!

354
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:32,270
Guess she just wanted a pillow.

355
00:07:34,150 --> 00:07:37,190
She's frowning in her sleep.

356
00:07:37,190 --> 00:07:40,230
She makes that face a lot, huh.

357
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:44,350
Hori- <i>san</i> , you're going to end up
with wrinkles on your forehead.

358
00:07:50,650 --> 00:07:55,230
She eats a lot, moves a lot,
and sleeps a lot.

359
00:07:55,230 --> 00:07:57,310
She's so funny.

360
00:07:58,730 --> 00:08:02,270
I hope these days never end.

361
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:04,060
Even after graduation.

362
00:08:08,270 --> 00:08:13,690
If that tiny happenstance
hadn't occurred...

363
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,480
If it hadn't...

364
00:08:21,650 --> 00:08:24,650
If it hadn't happened...

365
00:08:24,650 --> 00:08:28,060
Are our graduation essays due
on the last day of school?

366
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:29,900
Oh, crap, I totally forgot!

367
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:32,650
They took our graduation
picture super long ago, huh.

368
00:08:32,650 --> 00:08:34,560
I have no idea what I look like in mine.

369
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:37,900
I was next to a guy
I'd never spoken to before.

370
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:40,230
Ishikawa! Let's head home!

371
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:40,230
It was totally awkward. I don't
even remember if I said anything.

372
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:43,600
You're in the same class, though!

373
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,650
Sorry.

374
00:08:44,650 --> 00:08:47,400
Oh, it's okay.

375
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,690
You wanna go to karaoke today?

376
00:08:49,690 --> 00:08:51,480
How'd your sister do on that exam?

377
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,900
Didn't pass.

378
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:55,350
Oof. That sucks.

379
00:08:55,350 --> 00:08:56,940
Oh, Sengoku- <i>kun</i> !

380
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:58,020
Kono- <i>san</i> ?

381
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:59,230
I was just in the student council room...

382
00:08:59,230 --> 00:09:01,270
Oh, did you finish cleaning?

383
00:09:01,270 --> 00:09:03,270
Yeah, I did.

384
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:04,230
Got it.

385
00:09:04,230 --> 00:09:06,560
C'mon, Sakura, let's go!

386
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:08,350
Okay.

387
00:09:08,350 --> 00:09:12,350
She looked so much better with long hair.

388
00:09:12,350 --> 00:09:14,940
He's so unfriendly.

389
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:15,810
C'mon, hurry!

390
00:09:15,810 --> 00:09:19,270
Hey, Remi! Don't rush me!

391
00:09:19,270 --> 00:09:23,900
Oh, right! You know that shop
you told us about before?

392
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,810
Sakura?

393
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:28,100
Do you know them?

394
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:31,850
Huh? Oh, no, I don't.

395
00:09:41,810 --> 00:09:44,020
Taking my stuff home is such a pain...

396
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:47,650
Ugh, taking my stuff home is such a pain.

397
00:09:47,650 --> 00:09:49,980
I should've brought it home ages ago.

398
00:09:49,980 --> 00:09:54,150
I should've just brought it home ages ago.

399
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:59,660
All students, please head home
so the all-staff meeting may begin.

400
00:09:55,730 --> 00:09:58,770
Kyoko- <i>chan</i> ! Let's go!

401
00:09:58,770 --> 00:10:01,480
Yeah, I'm coming.

402
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:09,440
We have a whole 'nother
week until graduation...

403
00:10:10,810 --> 00:10:14,310
I hope it'll be warmer for graduation.

404
00:10:14,310 --> 00:10:16,400
For real.

405
00:10:19,850 --> 00:10:20,810
Kyoko- <i>chan</i> !

406
00:10:20,810 --> 00:10:23,770
Did you see that guy?!
He was a mega hottie!

407
00:10:23,770 --> 00:10:26,400
Wait, where? He a third year?!

408
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:28,980
Man, I didn't see!

409
00:10:32,060 --> 00:10:35,020
Whoa, someone's still here?

410
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:37,560
Gotta find my phone...

411
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:40,310
Whew, found it.

412
00:10:43,650 --> 00:10:45,270
Hey.

413
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:47,190
You dropped this.

414
00:10:47,190 --> 00:10:49,600
Huh? Wh-What?

415
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:53,230
This was on the floor.
Looks like an earring.

416
00:10:53,230 --> 00:10:54,440
Is it yours?

417
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,810
I-I don't know!

418
00:10:56,810 --> 00:10:58,650
Hey, dude!

419
00:10:58,650 --> 00:11:01,770
The hell? What a weirdo.

420
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:13,520
Somehow...

421
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:27,980
My high school days feel like
they amounted to nothing.

422
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:30,060
This is all hypothetical.

423
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:33,060
I know there's no point considering it.

424
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:36,770
But it wasn't hypothetical for you.

425
00:11:38,150 --> 00:11:40,150
Yeah.

426
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:46,980
Miyamura?

427
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:52,980
Sorry, I was spacing out.

428
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:57,560
You okay? What's got you all spaced out?

429
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,270
Just thinking.

430
00:12:01,270 --> 00:12:04,650
So many coincidences brought me here.

431
00:12:04,650 --> 00:12:09,270
What would it be like if
one of them didn't happen?

432
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:21,060
Sounds like the fact that we're here
together now is the work of fate.

433
00:12:22,650 --> 00:12:24,310
Maybe.

434
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:30,230
It was never completely
unfathomable, but it's real.

435
00:12:30,230 --> 00:12:33,350
You're here with me.

436
00:12:33,350 --> 00:12:35,770
Everyone is with me.

437
00:12:35,770 --> 00:12:39,230
I'm here with them now.

438
00:12:39,230 --> 00:12:44,730
Even if the "fate" you
mentioned doesn't really exist,

439
00:12:44,730 --> 00:12:50,310
I'm sure the world would slowly but surely

440
00:12:50,310 --> 00:12:52,730
move in the direction I want it to.

441
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:59,290
63rd Graduation Ceremony

442
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:59,600
Next, the farewell address from our
graduating student representative,

443
00:12:59,290 --> 00:13:01,550
Graduation

444
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:02,230
Kakeru Sengoku- <i>kun</i> .

445
00:13:02,230 --> 00:13:03,810
Yes, ma'am.

446
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:28,350
Nice going, me.

447
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:36,520
Hello, everyone.

448
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:39,270
Spring is upon us,

449
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:39,270
That dummy!

450
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:45,730
and so, too, is the graduation day for
the 63rd class of Katagiri High School.

451
00:13:47,350 --> 00:13:49,810
All graduating students,
please return to your classrooms.

452
00:13:49,810 --> 00:13:52,690
Miyamura- <i>kun</i> , you little punk!

453
00:13:52,690 --> 00:13:55,520
I'm sorry! I didn't do it on purpose!

454
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:56,650
Yo, Miyamura!

455
00:13:56,650 --> 00:13:57,810
Nice sneeze!

456
00:13:57,810 --> 00:13:59,650
It was <i>not nice</i> !

457
00:13:59,650 --> 00:14:02,270
He's so scary!

458
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:03,850
Sorry, Ishikawa- <i>kun</i> !

459
00:14:03,850 --> 00:14:05,310
Shoot, I lost him!

460
00:14:05,310 --> 00:14:09,850
C'mon, dude, should the graduating student
speaker be sprinting through the halls?

461
00:14:09,850 --> 00:14:12,980
Nice speech, by the way.

462
00:14:12,980 --> 00:14:15,650
So what were you chasing Miyamura for?

463
00:14:15,650 --> 00:14:18,310
What do you <i>think</i> I was chasing him for?!

464
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:25,600
I've gotta apologize to him later.

465
00:14:33,730 --> 00:14:35,770
Nice day out.

466
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,350
You're having fun.

467
00:14:42,350 --> 00:14:43,520
Yup.

468
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:45,350
You cut your hair.

469
00:14:45,350 --> 00:14:49,020
They found out about the
piercings. And my tattoos.

470
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:53,190
I have a lot of friends,
plus a girlfriend.

471
00:14:57,020 --> 00:15:00,980
You finally looked at me.

472
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,100
Sorry.

473
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:07,940
I promise I won't pretend
you're not there anymore.

474
00:15:12,190 --> 00:15:14,190
I'll disappear for you.

475
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:21,730
Congrats on graduating.

476
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:28,270
There he is! C'mon, Miyamura,
we're gonna take a class photo!

477
00:15:28,270 --> 00:15:30,440
You gotta hurry back, or...

478
00:15:31,980 --> 00:15:34,600
What's up?

479
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,400
Nothing.

480
00:15:38,190 --> 00:15:40,940
The wind's so strong today.

481
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:45,690
Ugh, where the hell is our class?

482
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,540
m 942 2 l 1162 2 1162 56 942 56

483
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,540
Photo Duty

484
00:15:45,690 --> 00:15:47,520
Sensei, let's take a picture together!

485
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,520
I want one, too!

486
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:52,520
Aww, well, okay, I guess.

487
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:56,650
You're supposed to take
pictures of <i>all</i> of us, Yasuda!

488
00:15:56,650 --> 00:15:59,100
Why would I take pictures of guys?

489
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:03,190
I'll grab a snapshot of you
with my eyes. There, done.

490
00:16:03,190 --> 00:16:07,310
Oh, come on! This is a big life moment!
Get a picture of us, please!

491
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:08,940
Hori- <i>senpai</i> !

492
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:12,600
I'm so sad I won't get to see you anymore!

493
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,770
What's up?

494
00:16:13,770 --> 00:16:16,850
Y-You can still come over to see me!

495
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:18,480
Really?!

496
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:20,230
Not too often, though!

497
00:16:20,230 --> 00:16:21,600
It's her last day.

498
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:24,100
Might as well let her have it, then.

499
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,900
Our last day, huh...

500
00:16:34,730 --> 00:16:37,560
I'm looking for Remi, have you seen her?

501
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:41,020
Oh, Ayasaki? No, I haven't.

502
00:16:41,020 --> 00:16:42,690
Oh.

503
00:16:44,730 --> 00:16:46,770
Hey, so...

504
00:16:46,770 --> 00:16:52,980
So, uh-- Sorry, I just...

505
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,230
Thank you.

506
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:02,770
I had so much fun this year. Really.

507
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:04,980
I had the best time of my life,

508
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:07,900
and part of that was
because of you, Ishikawa- <i>kun</i> .

509
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:12,150
I like you, Ishikawa- <i>kun</i> .
And I like Yoshikawa- <i>san</i> , too.

510
00:17:12,150 --> 00:17:14,690
I'll never forget you.

511
00:17:14,690 --> 00:17:17,940
Same. Neither will I.

512
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:21,770
Well, good. Thanks.

513
00:17:21,770 --> 00:17:23,770
Yeah, same.

514
00:17:23,770 --> 00:17:25,400
Bye, then!

515
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:28,060
Take care. See you again soon!

516
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:29,980
See you later!

517
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:38,150
Guess she's trying to leave
her feelings behind at school.

518
00:17:38,150 --> 00:17:40,060
Goodbye.

519
00:17:42,290 --> 00:17:44,250
BA-DUMP

520
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:45,190
Oh! Congratulations on graduating!

521
00:17:45,190 --> 00:17:48,400
Hey, you graduated, too! Congrats!

522
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,480
Thank you!

523
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:53,310
Oh, right! I needed to tell you something.

524
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:55,150
Wh-What?!

525
00:17:53,550 --> 00:17:54,800
BA-DUMP

526
00:17:55,150 --> 00:17:58,690
I'd like to go somewhere
with everyone after graduation.

527
00:17:58,690 --> 00:17:59,650
You mean as a group?

528
00:17:59,650 --> 00:18:04,810
Yeah. We had this conversation
with the student council the other day.

529
00:18:04,810 --> 00:18:06,600
It made me think, once I get my license...

530
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:08,650
All of us best buds could travel!

531
00:18:08,650 --> 00:18:13,850
We'll take Miyamura- <i>kun</i> ,
Hori- <i>san</i> , Kono- <i>san</i> ...

532
00:18:09,150 --> 00:18:11,350
Best buds.

533
00:18:11,350 --> 00:18:13,850
Just the same as always.

534
00:18:13,850 --> 00:18:14,520
Sure.

535
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:15,350
Huh?

536
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:17,230
Sounds great! Let's do it!

537
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:18,100
Oh, good!

538
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:19,600
Thanks for offering to drive!

539
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:20,650
Huh?

540
00:18:20,650 --> 00:18:25,310
Nothing's going to change after
graduation, and if it does, that's fine.

541
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:27,900
We'll still be friends.

542
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:30,190
Now there's my special boy!

543
00:18:30,190 --> 00:18:32,270
Kyosuke- <i>san</i> !

544
00:18:32,270 --> 00:18:33,810
Whoa, is that Miyamura- <i>kun</i> 's dad?!

545
00:18:33,810 --> 00:18:34,690
He's so young!

546
00:18:34,690 --> 00:18:36,230
They look so similar!

547
00:18:36,230 --> 00:18:38,440
Similar <i>how</i> ?

548
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:41,270
I wanna get a picture
with my wonderful kid!

549
00:18:41,270 --> 00:18:43,770
Okay, let me get Hori- <i>san</i> --

550
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:49,100
Why the hell are you here, Dad?! Huh?!

551
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:51,020
I'm here to have Dad fun!

552
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:54,400
Get out of here before someone
sees you in this ridiculous outfit!

553
00:18:55,850 --> 00:18:58,690
Miyamura! Where's <i>your</i> mom and dad?!

554
00:18:58,690 --> 00:19:01,770
They were here for a bit,
but had to head home for work.

555
00:19:01,770 --> 00:19:04,150
Man, why you gotta be so mad?

556
00:19:04,150 --> 00:19:07,730
Shut up and get lost!

557
00:19:07,730 --> 00:19:11,600
C-C'mon, now...

558
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:12,650
Okay, you're good!

559
00:19:12,650 --> 00:19:14,480
You serious, Iura?

560
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,560
Dead serious, dude.

561
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:17,060
Big brother!

562
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:19,020
Hey, Moto, you came?

563
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:19,520
Yeah.

564
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:21,900
Whoa, is this your little sister?

565
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:23,060
Yup!

566
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:24,850
You come to pick your big brother up?

567
00:19:24,850 --> 00:19:28,690
Mom said she wanted you home early.

568
00:19:28,690 --> 00:19:31,480
Plus I figured I could see what
my new school would be like.

569
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,560
Wow, really?!

570
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:36,600
God, that ceremony was so long!
Why'd they talk so much?

571
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:40,230
Okey-dokey, let's get
our butts home, Moto!

572
00:19:40,230 --> 00:19:43,690
That's all, folks! Bye bye!

573
00:19:43,690 --> 00:19:45,980
Nice to see Iura peppy till the end.

574
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:48,020
All's right with the world.

575
00:19:51,810 --> 00:19:52,940
Big brother.

576
00:19:52,940 --> 00:19:55,100
Yes, little sister?

577
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,980
Is it really you?

578
00:19:56,980 --> 00:19:58,900
Yep, it's me.

579
00:20:03,850 --> 00:20:05,520
Miyamura!

580
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:09,060
We're gonna go get sushi, wanna come?!

581
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:10,440
I'm in!

582
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:12,400
Sweet! Let's head out, then.

583
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:15,150
Kyosuke's gonna be so thrilled,
like, annoyingly so.

584
00:20:15,150 --> 00:20:16,600
Okay!

585
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:19,900
There's no distance between us.

586
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:24,100
I've never been this
close to a person before.

587
00:20:25,150 --> 00:20:27,480
There's no boundary between us.

588
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:30,770
I used to be terrified of that.

589
00:20:30,770 --> 00:20:34,020
I was so scared of this, Hori- <i>san</i> .

590
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:36,020
You know,

591
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:37,900
I had no idea

592
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,770
that I could feel

593
00:20:40,770 --> 00:20:42,770
so many different emotions.

594
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:47,190
I don't think either of us knew

595
00:20:47,190 --> 00:20:51,810
how scary or nerve-wracking being
yourself around others could be.

596
00:20:51,810 --> 00:20:56,100
But you made me realize all of it.

597
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:59,850
What can I do for you?

598
00:20:59,850 --> 00:21:03,520
How can I make you smile?

599
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:07,770
You're so much stronger
than I think you are,

600
00:21:07,770 --> 00:21:13,150
and you're so much weaker
than I feel you are.

601
00:21:13,150 --> 00:21:15,440
You're delicate.

602
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,600
You're fragile.

603
00:21:19,810 --> 00:21:25,060
That's why wherever you go,
bright, sunny days follow after.

604
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:30,980
For years, the only person
I knew this well was myself.

605
00:21:32,650 --> 00:21:37,600
I never knew a world
like this even existed.

606
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:41,940
Thank you for shattering my reality.

607
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:47,520
Thank you for wanting a future with me.

608
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:53,730
What can I do for <i>you</i> ?

609
00:21:53,730 --> 00:21:56,730
How can I repay you for what you've done?

610
00:21:58,730 --> 00:22:01,940
C'mon, Miyamura!

611
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:09,850
Oh.

612
00:22:09,850 --> 00:22:13,520
The spring sky is bluer
than I've ever seen.

613
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:19,770
If only I could gift you
this wonderful sky.

614
00:22:19,770 --> 00:22:24,560
No, I know what you'd like better.

615
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:29,690
A cake with lots of whipped cream on top.

